# JakeOS Phase 3.2 — environment secrets
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (no extension prefix), fill in the four values,
# and DO NOT commit `.env` to git.  The .gitignore in this folder excludes
# .env automatically.
#
# How to get each value:
#
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN
#   The token Cloudflare gave you when you created the tunnel in
#   https://one.dash.cloudflare.com → Networks → Tunnels.  It's the
#   long string from the docker-run command Cloudflare displayed.
#
# OAUTH2_PROXY_CLIENT_ID  /  OAUTH2_PROXY_CLIENT_SECRET
#   From https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials → your
#   OAuth 2.0 Client.  Two separate values.
#
# OAUTH2_PROXY_COOKIE_SECRET
#   Must be a string of exactly 16, 24, or 32 ASCII characters
#   (oauth2-proxy uses it as a raw AES key, NOT base64-decoded).
#   Generate one with:
#
#       openssl rand -hex 16     # 32 hex chars = 32 ASCII bytes (recommended)
#
#   Don't use `openssl rand -base64 32` — that gives 44 chars, which
#   oauth2-proxy will reject.  Don't reuse this between projects.

CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=

OAUTH2_PROXY_CLIENT_ID=
OAUTH2_PROXY_CLIENT_SECRET=
OAUTH2_PROXY_COOKIE_SECRET=
